---
import ContentLayout from "@/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumb from "@/components/ui/Breadcrumb.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@/config/site";

const updated = "26 July 2026";
---

<ContentLayout
  meta={{
    title: "Privacy Policy",
    description:
      "How Qinobee approaches the collection, use and protection of personal information.",
    canonical: "/privacy",
  }}
>
  <Breadcrumb items={[{ name: "Home", href: "/" }, { name: "Privacy" }]} />

  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: {updated}</em></p>

  <p>
    <strong>This page is provided for general information only and is not
    legal advice.</strong> It describes our intended approach to privacy in
    plain language. For advice about your specific circumstances, please
    consult a qualified professional.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>
    We collect information you provide directly, such as your name and contact
    details when you request a demo or get in touch. We also collect basic
    technical information, such as pages visited, to help us understand how the
    site is used and to keep it working well.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <p>
    We use the information we collect to respond to your enquiries, to provide
    and improve our services, and to communicate with you about things you have
    asked us about. We do not sell your personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>How we protect information</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable steps to protect personal information against loss,
    misuse and unauthorised access. No method of transmission or storage is
    completely secure, but we work to safeguard the information entrusted to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You may ask us to access, correct or delete the personal information we hold
    about you, subject to any legal obligations we have to retain it. To make a
    request, contact us using the details below.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about this policy, please email
    <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a>.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
